        "For a DP2 student in the middle of Higher Level Chemistry, an Extended Essay and CAS commitments, an additional compulsory Thai-language and social-studies timetable is a real constraint rather than a formality. It is one of the clearest differences between a Thai national's experience of the Diploma Programme and an expatriate classmate's, and schools vary in how tightly they enforce and schedule it, so it is worth confirming directly with your child's school rather than assuming a single national standard applies everywhere.",
